# <%= current_page.data.title %>

This guidance applies to non-production and production environments where relevant. Production approvals and readiness checks remain part of [Path to Live](/cloud-native-platform/path-to-live/).

## Purpose

## Configuration

We use [Azure Front Door](https://azure.microsoft.com/en-gb/services/frontdoor/) as our entry point
into the HMCTS estate.

### CFT

Configuration is located in
[azure-platform-terraform](https://github.com/hmcts/azure-platform-terraform/blob/master/environments/prod/prod.tfvars).
A minimal configuration for production would be:

```hcl
{
	product                     = "product"
	name                        = "app-name"
	custom_domain               = "your-app.service.gov.uk"
	backend_domain              = ["firewall-prod-int-palo-cftprod.uksouth.cloudapp.azure.com"]
	dns_zone_name               = "your-app.service.gov.uk"
}
```

### SDS

Configuration is located in
[sds-azure-platform](https://github.com/hmcts/sds-azure-platform/blob/master/environments/prod/prod.tfvars).
A minimal configuration for production would be:

```hcl
{
	name             = "app-name"
	custom_domain    = "your-app.service.gov.uk"
	backend_domain   = ["firewall-prod-int-palo-sdsprod.uksouth.cloudapp.azure.com"]
	dns_zone_name    = "your-app.service.gov.uk"
}
```

For other options, look at what existing applications use in the same file.

### TLS certificate

You do not need to supply a certificate. By default Front Door issues and renews a managed
certificate for your custom domain, and the pipeline adds the record that validates it to your DNS zone.

A certificate from Key Vault is only used when an entry sets `ssl_mode = "AzureKeyVault"`. The
certificate named in `certificate_name` must then already be in the platform's Key Vault, or the
build fails. Many existing entries have `certificate_name` without `ssl_mode`; it has no effect there,
so leave it out when you copy one. If you think you need a Key Vault certificate, ask in
[#platops-help](https://hmcts-reform.slack.com/app_redirect?channel=platops-help).

If your domain's DNS is hosted outside the HMCTS [public DNS](public-dns.html), the entry sets
`hosted_externally = true` and the validation record has to be added with your DNS provider instead.
Ask in #platops-help for the value.

### Raise the pull request

Make sure your [DNS pull request](public-dns.html) has been merged first. The build looks up the
zone named in `dns_zone_name` and fails if it does not exist.

Then send a pull request with your configuration change,
you can ask for review in [#platops-code-review](https://hmcts-reform.slack.com/app_redirect?channel=platops-code-review).

